  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Propanal and methanal undergo aldol condensation reaction with sodium hydroxide. The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></math>-unsaturated compound undergo&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></math>conjugated addition with cyanide ion gives a racemic&nbsp;mixture. The cyanide undergo acidic hydrolysis gives carboxylic acid.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0058_5f7cb37a8acf.png\" style=\"width: 615px; height: 465px;\" /></p><p>Carboxylic acid will give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gas, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaHCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> solution</p>"
